# Developing {{ app_slug }}

A **tenant** of a shared k3s cluster. Flux owns everything under
`kubernetes/flux/`: edit YAML, open a {{ change_request }}, and on merge to
`main` the operator-side Flux `Kustomization` reconciles this repo into
`{{ app_namespace }}`. There is no `kubectl apply` / `helm upgrade` in the normal
flow.

Read the hard rules in [`CLAUDE.md`](../../../CLAUDE.md#hard-rules) before any change.

## Local loop

```bash
task lint                 # every gate that runs locally
task render               # exactly what Flux will apply
{% if enable_image_build %}task build                # docker build
{% endif %}```

Secret detection runs {% if ci_shape == 'none' %}only in the pre-commit hooks{% else %}in the pipeline and in the pre-commit hooks{% endif %}, so run
`pre-commit install` once. Fix lint before opening the {{ change_request }}.

## Deploy + verify

Merging to `main` triggers a reconcile (a short git poll is the fallback). With a
kubeconfig from the operator on `KUBECONFIG` — read on `{{ app_namespace }}` and
on `flux-system`:

```bash
task flux:status          # flux get kustomization {{ app_slug }}
task flux:reconcile       # force an immediate reconcile
{% if secrets_backend != 'none' %}task secrets:check        # ExternalSecret sync state
{% endif %}kubectl get pods -n {{ app_namespace }}
```

`task flux:reconcile` also needs annotate and patch on the Kustomization and its
GitRepository; a read-only kubeconfig refuses it.

If a change did not take: check the Kustomization is `Ready`, then the workload.
The usual causes are a failing `kustomize build` (CI would have caught it), an
`ExternalSecret` waiting on a store the operator has not wired yet, or an image
tag that does not exist in the registry.

